   <refbody>    <section>
      <p>This API request includes the following path and header parameters.</p>
      <ul id="ul_104927175">
         <li>
            <b>Path parameters:</b>
         </li>
         <li>The path parameters of the request URL path act as a placeholder for the sensor ID value.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
         <tgroup cols="4">
            <colspec colname="c1"/>
            <colspec colname="c2"/>
            <colspec colname="c3"/>
            <colspec colname="c4"/>
            <tbody>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Parameter</b>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Type</b>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Description</b>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Required</b>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>sensorId</entry>
                  <entry>string</entry>
                  <entry>Sensor ID</entry>
                  <entry>Yes</entry>
               </row>
            </tbody>
         </tgroup>
      </table>
    <section>
      <ul id="ul_104927176">
         <li>
            <b>Header</b>
            <b>Parameters</b>
            <b>:</b>
         </li>
      </ul>
      <p>The header parameters provide instructions to the API on handling the request, such as authentication and compressing responses over 1KB.</p>
    </section>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
         <tgroup cols="5">
            <colspec colname="c1"/>
            <colspec colname="c2"/>
            <colspec colname="c3"/>
            <colspec colname="c4"/>
            <colspec colname="c5"/>
            <tbody>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Parameter</b>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Type</b>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Description</b>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Input Value</b>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Required</b>
                  </entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>Authorization</entry>
                  <entry>string</entry>
                  <entry>Authenticates API requests. Provide a valid bearer token in the HTTP header. This bearer token can be obtained from the <xref href="../access_the_api/oauth.dita" format="dita">OAuth bearer token request</xref>.</entry>
                  <entry>N/A</entry>
                  <entry>Yes</entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>Accept-Encoding</entry>
                  <entry>string</entry>
                  <entry>Accept-Encoding. Must be set to: gzip deflate Br Responses over 1KB in size will automatically be compressed. The client must be capable of receiving and decompressing the response. Warning: If this header is not set, responses greater than 1KB will fail.</entry>
                  <entry>N/A</entry>
                  <entry>Yes</entry>
               </row>
            </tbody>
         </tgroup>
      </table></refbody>
